---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import AudioReader from '../components/AudioReader.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
import '../styles/home.css';
import { projects } from '../data/projects';
import { readingMinutes as readTime } from '../utils/publication';
const posts = (await getCollection('blog')).sort((a,b) => b.data.pubDate.valueOf()-a.data.pubDate.valueOf() || b.id.localeCompare(a.id));
const papers = posts.filter(p => p.data.kind === 'research').slice(0,3);
const lead = posts.find(p => p.id === 'the-question-behind-the-work')!;
const notes = posts.filter(p => p.data.kind === 'note' && p.id !== lead.id).slice(0,2);
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head><BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION}/></head>
  <body>
    <div class="site-shell">
      <Header/>
      <main id="top">
        <div class="issue-line"><span>A personal notebook, made public</span><span>Security / Systems / Sovereignty</span><span>Issue 01 — September 2026</span></div>
        <section class="cover" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
          <div class="cover-copy" id="introduction">
            <p class="eyebrow">The person behind the pages</p>
            <h1 id="hero-title">I’m Iefan.<br/>I build, question,<br/>and <em>connect.</em></h1>
            <p class="cover-deck">An independent engineer exploring the space between secure systems and a more sovereign digital life.</p>
            <p class="cover-bio">My work moves between software and hardware: cryptography, embedded devices, decentralized protocols, and intelligence at the edge. This is where I share the questions, ideas, and experiments along the way.</p>
            <div data-no-narration><AudioReader target="#introduction" label="A short introduction" compact/></div>
            <div class="cover-links" data-no-narration><a href="/research/">Browse the research <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="/work/">Visit the workbench <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
          </div>
          <aside class="cover-story" aria-labelledby="cover-story-title">
            <div class="cover-art" role="img" aria-label="Intersecting blue forms representing hardware, protocols, and human agency">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 480 440" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                <defs><pattern id="engraving" width="6" height="6" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M0 0V6" stroke="#f6f5ef" stroke-width="1"/></pattern><clipPath id="arch"><path d="M75 350V180C75 25 305 25 305 180V350Z"/></clipPath></defs>
                <rect width="480" height="440" fill="#e7eaf3"/>
                <g stroke="#c7ccdf" stroke-width="1"><path d="M30 30H450V410H30Z"/><path d="M30 110H450M30 190H450M30 270H450M30 350H450M110 30V410M190 30V410M270 30V410M350 30V410M430 30V410"/></g>
                <path d="M75 350V180C75 25 305 25 305 180V350Z" fill="#2949ba"/>
                <rect x="70" y="50" width="245" height="305" fill="url(#engraving)" clip-path="url(#arch)"/>
                <circle cx="300" cy="254" r="122" fill="#f6f5ef"/>
                <circle cx="300" cy="254" r="84" fill="#20231f"/>
                <circle cx="300" cy="254" r="48" fill="#f6f5ef"/>
                <path d="M190 76V385M52 254H427" stroke="#7684b3" stroke-dasharray="4 6"/>
                <circle cx="190" cy="254" r="6" fill="#f6f5ef" stroke="#2949ba"/>
                <g fill="#56608c" font-family="monospace" font-size="9"><text x="40" y="52">01 / HARDWARE</text><text x="326" y="400">02 / HUMAN AGENCY</text><text x="325" y="53">FIG. 001</text></g>
              </svg>
              <div class="art-credit"><span>At the intersection of things.</span><span>Study No. 01</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="cover-story-heading"><p class="eyebrow">The opening essay</p><span>{readTime(lead.body)} min read</span></div>
            <h2 id="cover-story-title"><a href={`/blog/${lead.id}/`}>The question<br/> behind the work.</a></h2>
            <p>Who gets to decide what our technology does — and what would it take to make that choice ours?</p>
            <a class="text-link" href={`/blog/${lead.id}/`}>Read the essay <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </aside>
        </section>
        <section class="editor-letter" id="practice" aria-labelledby="letter-title">
          <div><p class="eyebrow">A note to the reader</p><span class="letter-signature">Iefan.</span></div>
          <div><h2 id="letter-title">Follow the question.<br/>Even when it crosses disciplines.</h2><p>I’m drawn to problems that don’t fit neatly into a single layer. A privacy decision becomes a protocol decision. A protocol depends on a device. A device eventually meets a person.</p><p>This publication follows those connections. Some pages are practical engineering notes; others are research proposals with assumptions still to test. The aim is to make the thinking visible.</p></div>
          <aside><span class="small-label">The recurring question</span><blockquote>“How do we build technology that gives people more agency?”</blockquote><a class="text-link" href="mailto:iefan.work@gmail.com">Write to me <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></aside>
        </section>
        <section class="research-section" id="research" aria-labelledby="research-title">
          <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / Open investigations</p><h2 id="research-title">On the research desk.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/research/">All working papers <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
          <p class="section-deck">Questions made concrete. Proposals with explicit assumptions and a path to validation.</p>
          <div class="paper-grid">{papers.map((post,i) => <article class="paper-card"><div class="paper-top"><span>0{i+1}</span><span>{post.data.topics[0]}</span></div><h3><a href={`/blog/${post.id}/`}>{post.data.title}</a></h3><p>{post.data.description}</p><div class="paper-bottom"><span>Draft proposal · {readTime(post.body)} min</span><a href={`/blog/${post.id}/`} aria-label={`Read ${post.data.title}`}>↗</a></div></article>)}</div>
        </section>
        <section class="journal-section" aria-labelledby="journal-title">
          <div class="journal-intro"><p class="eyebrow">02 / The journal</p><h2 id="journal-title">Thinking<br/> out loud.</h2><p>Project stories, engineering decisions, and lessons from the workbench.</p><a class="text-link" href="/blog/">The complete journal <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
          <div class="journal-entries">{notes.map(post => <article><div class="entry-meta"><span>{post.data.topics[0]}</span><span>{readTime(post.body)} min read</span></div><h3><a href={`/blog/${post.id}/`}>{post.data.title}</a></h3><p>{post.data.description}</p><a class="text-link" href={`/blog/${post.id}/`}>Read the note <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>)}</div>
        </section>
        <section class="work-section" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
          <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / Away from the page</p><h2 id="work-title">At the workbench.</h2></div><span class="section-aside">Ideas, in contact with the real world.</span></div>
          <div class="work-list">{projects.map((project, index) => <article><span class="work-number">0{index + 1}</span><div><span class="small-label">{project.field}</span><h3><a href={`/work/#${project.id}`}>{project.name}</a></h3></div><p>{project.description}</p><a class="text-link" href={`/blog/${project.article}/`}>Read the case study <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>)}</div>
          <a class="text-link work-index-link" href="/work/">Explore the full workbench <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </section>
        <section class="practice-notes" aria-labelledby="practice-notes-title">
          <div><p class="eyebrow">A thread through the work</p><h2 id="practice-notes-title">What makes a system<br/>worth building?</h2></div>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>A choice that stays yours.</dt><dd>Privacy and ownership matter most when they become decisions people can understand and act on.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Care at the boundaries.</dt><dd>The interesting failures happen between layers: a key and a device, a payment and access, a document and a voice.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>A question you can test.</dt><dd>A promising idea needs explicit assumptions, a useful experiment, and room for the result to change the design.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </section>
        <section class="contact" id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-title"><p class="eyebrow">The conversation continues</p><div><h2 id="contact-title">Have a question<br/>worth following?</h2><p>Ideas, thoughtful disagreements, and difficult systems problems are all welcome.<a href="mailto:iefan.work@gmail.com" data-testid="home-contact-email-link">iefan.work@gmail.com <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p></div></section>
      </main>
      <Footer folio="home"/>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
